devices  The  command can be used to inspect and reconfigure High
Definition Audio devices and their child codecs.   The  mandatory
argument  specifies  the action to take.  Valid commands are: For
each child codec of the chosen device, display the  nid,  vendor,
product, subsystem and device IDs.  Retrieve and display the cur‐
rent  codec  configuration  in human‐readable form.  Retrieve and
display the current codec configuration as a XML  plist.   Detach
the  specified  codec and then re‐attach with its widgets explic‐
itly configured according to the specified plist.  If no plist is
given, the in‐built widget parsing rules based on the High Defin‐
ition Audio specification will be used.  Output a DOT file  suit‐
able  processing  by  graphviz.  The resulting image will graphi‐
cally show the structure and interconnections of the widgets that
form the chosen codec.  control devices  The  command  first  ap‐
peared in is based on two separate programs written by under con‐
tract  by  Integration  into  one program and writing this manual
page was done by When a plist is loaded and the codec reattaches,
all mixer controls will be returned to their default values.
